        "title": "Science and Religion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The \"conflict thesis\" — science and religion are at war — is the dominant popular\nnarrative. Historians of science have spent 40 years dismantling it. The actual\nhistory is complicated. The current intellectual frontier is cognitive science of\nreligion: not \"does religion conflict with science?\" but \"what cognitive mechanisms\nproduce religion, and what does that imply?\""
    },
    {
      "id": "07-SCIENCE-RELIGION.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-SCIENCE-RELIGION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:religious-studies:07-science-religion, git-history:religious-studies:07-science-religion]",
        "canonical_path": "religious-studies/07-SCIENCE-RELIGION.md",
        "concepts": "[science, religion]",
        "current_path": "religious-studies/07-SCIENCE-RELIGION.md",
        "id": "maxim:religious-studies:science-religion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "religious-studies",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[science, religion]",
        "section": "religious-studies",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Science and Religion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              SCIENCE-RELIGION INTERFACE — CONCEPTUAL MAP             |\n|                                                                      |\n|  HISTORICAL QUESTION:          DEMARCATION QUESTION:                 |\n|  Did/do they conflict?         Are they even the same type of        |\n|  Did science replace religion? inquiry? (NOMA vs. overlap)           |\n|                                                                      |\n|  SPECIFIC SCIENCE INTERFACE:   COGNITIVE QUESTION:                   |\n|  Evolution vs. creation        Why does religion exist?              |\n|  Cosmology vs. cosmogony       What cognitive mechanisms produce it? |\n|  Neuroscience vs. soul         Is it adaptive or a byproduct?        |\n|                                                                      |\n|  BARBOUR'S TAXONOMY:                                                 |\n|  Conflict (Dawkins) -> Independence (NOMA/Gould) ->                  |\n|  Dialogue (shared questions) -> Integration (Process theology)       |\n|                                                                      |\n|  STATUS OF CONFLICT THESIS: Historians reject it as ideology.        |\n|  STATUS OF NOMA: Philosophically thin but pragmatically useful.      |\n|  STATUS OF CSR: Active research program; most productive frontier.   |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
